{# This is the LLMT Template for generating user story files #}
{# It must be redered following the instructions defined in the `../../agile-ddd-update/references/LLMT-COMPILER.md` file #}
{# MANDATORY: the {{ id }} is a 6-digit ID (with leading zeroes) and {{ name }} is the story name (lowercase, hyphens). Example: `st-000001-vite-migration` #}
# st-{{ id }}: {{ name }}
{# This is the Feature this story belongs to #}
# Feature: ft-{{ featureId }}: {{ featureName }}

## User Story

As a {{ persona }},

I want to {{ action }},

so that {{ value }}.

## Acceptance Criteria

{% for scenario in scenarios %}
### Scenario-{{ scenario.id }}: {{ scenario.name }}
```
Given {{ scenario.context }}
When {{ scenario.action }}
Then {{ scenario.result }}
```

{% endfor %}

## Non-Negotiable Tests
{# Inmutable scenarios, see ../references/NON-NEGOTIABLE-TESTS.md #}

{% for test in nonNegotiableTests %}
### NNT-{{ test.id }}: {{ test.name }}
```
Given {{ test.context }}
When {{ test.action }}
Then {{ test.result }}
```

{% endfor %}

## Status

{# Feature status - Default to NOT-STARTED #}
**{{ status }}**

## Dependencies
{# Dependent user stories #}
{# A table with columns: ID, STATUS, Title
Example:
| ID     | STATUS        | Title                          |
|--------|---------------|--------------------------------|
| st-000000 | DONE          | This is the first user story   |
| st-000001 | IN-PROGRESS   | This is the second user story  |
| st-000002 | NOT-STARTED   | This is the third user story   |
...
| st-00000N | NOT-STARTED   | This is the last user story    |
#}

| ID     | STATUS        | Title                          |
|--------|---------------|--------------------------------|
{% for userStory in dependentStories %}
| {{ userStory.id }} | {{ userStory.status }} | {{ userStory.title }} |
{% endfor %}

## Comments
{# Optional: Comments from agents or user, it must be brief and concise #}
{# A table with columns:
    - Agent: [agentName] like `/agile-story-add` or `/agile-story-start` or [userName]
    - Coding Agent: [codingAgent] like `Cursor`, `Codex`, `Claude Code`, `Pi`, `others`]
    - Datetime: [date] in format `YYYY-MM-DD - HH:MM:SS` like `2000-01-01 - 12:00:00`
    - Comment: [comment] like `Added this story` or `User updated this story` or `Sliced this story`
Example:
| Agent                    | Coding Agent  | Datetime              | Comment                |
|--------------------------|---------------|-----------------------|------------------------|
| `/agile-story-add`       | `Codex`       | 2000-01-01 - 12:00:00 | Added this user story |
| `User`                   | `Cursor`      | 2000-01-01 - 12:00:00 | User updated this user story |
| `/agile-story-start`     | `Pi`          | 2000-01-01 - 12:00:00 | Started working on this user story |
| `/agile-story-in-review` | `Claude Code` | 2000-01-01 - 12:00:00 | User story is in review |
| `/agile-story-done`      | `Pi`          | 2000-01-01 - 12:00:00 | User story is done |
#}

| Agent                    | Coding Agent  | Datetime              | Comment                |
|--------------------------|---------------|-----------------------|------------------------|
{% for comment in comments %}
| {{ comment.agent }} | {{ comment.codingAgent }} | {{ comment.datetime }} | {{ comment.comment }} |
{% endfor %}
